cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hyperproc: readers, atmospheric, topographic and BRDF correction for imaging spectrometers"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ji
    given-names: Fujiang
    email: fujiang.ji@wisc.edu
    affiliation: "University of Wisconsin-Madison"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # <- fill this in
repository-code: "https://github.com/FujiangJi/hyperproc"
url: "https://github.com/FujiangJi/hyperproc"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for processing imaging-spectrometer data from raw radiance to
  analysis-ready reflectance. Readers for eleven airborne and satellite
  instruments return one uniform xarray contract; ISOFIT-driven atmospheric
  correction, topographic correction and two BRDF routes (MODIS c-factor for
  satellites, fitted kernel models for airborne flightline groups) run on top of
  it, alongside spectral transforms, resampling, a unified quality layer and
  coregistration.
keywords:
  - imaging spectroscopy
  - hyperspectral
  - remote sensing
  - atmospheric correction
  - BRDF
  - topographic correction
  - ISOFIT
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
